## Next existing integration step, not a new policy gate

Gate 5 overall is not complete. Read-only source review identified the concrete
remaining connection:

1. `run_sft_release_gate_fixture_v1.watch_parent` passes generated `TREE` and
   `DECLARED` stand-ins to `VerifiedRelease`. The existing manifest requires
   `runtime/`, `dependencies/`, `source/`; the accepted OCI uses `/usr/local`,
   `/usr/lib` and `/opt/lumi-release/source` with separate lock/base/source
   controls. Its observer report cannot simply be relabelled a release-tree
   verification receipt.
2. The existing guardian release callback must be controlled by verification of
   that actual accepted software identity before ML starts. That trusted identity
   must reach the worker/controller rather than the fixture's synthetic `admit`
   callback and `source_identity_sha256="f" * 64`. `WorkerRun.run` already has an
   admission seam; Supervisor resource accounting does not authenticate software.
3. This connection needs its own bounded remote integration verification before
   claiming guardian-integrated acceptance. No implementation or native run for
   this next step occurred here. The public real-worker admission remains closed.

Preserve the accepted work and existing data, rights, training-profile and
resource constraints while completing this wiring. Dedicated host/S3/data
binding and approved H100/CUDA validation remain downstream. Do not treat the
old FSDP/context-4096 draft as supported by the current DDP worker automatically.

The Mac performed lightweight source/metadata reads only. No local native/ML
execution, image or wheel download, GPU/instance action, S3/SSH, real model/data
read, training, registry mutation, dataset seal or production promotion occurred.
This result-only document must not be pushed merely to trigger another CI run.
